# 2. Positive Q-values indicate actions expected to give better future rewards, while low or negative values indicate less useful actions.
# 3. The agent explores the maze using random actions and gradually learns from the rewards it receives.
# 4. Moving into a wall or outside the maze gives a penalty of -10, moving to an empty cell gives -1, and reaching the goal gives +100.
# 5. The learned path displays the sequence of maze coordinates followed by the agent from the start position.
